--- !u!114 &33731102
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 33731100}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 30e8e37d88289204784a0442b3c88612, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - Connect (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of all used modules to the
    (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board.
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the PV Solar Panel (Comm. Out) to the Main Control
    Board module (Comm. In).
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the Wind Turbine (Comm. in) to the Main Control
    Board module (Comm. out).
  - Connect Dump Load terminals of the Wind/Solar Hybrid System Controller module
    to the terminals of the Dump Load 400W module.
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) Battery Input terminals of the Wind/Solar Hybrid System
    Controller module to (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the Battery 24 V / 9 Ah module.
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) Battery Input terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module
    to (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the Battery 24 V / 9 Ah module.
  - Connect (L1), (L2), and (L3) terminals of the Generator Output from the Wind
    Turbine module to (U), (V), and (W) terminals of the Wind Input of the Wind/Solar
    Hybrid System Controller module.
  - Connect (L) and (N) AC Output terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module to (L)
    and (N) terminals of the AC Halogen Lamp and AC LED Lamp modules.
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) Solar Input terminals of the Wind/Solar Hybrid System
    Controller module to (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the PV Solar Panel Output module.
  - Release the emergency stop button on the main board.
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the main board.
  - Switch on the main board ON/OFF switch.
  - Release the emergency button of the PV Solar Panel.
  - Switch on the PV Solar Panel ON/OFF.
  - "Switch the Run/Stop selector to\_Run\_state."
  - Switch to the software monitor
  - Press the Enable button.
  - Release the emergency button on the wind turbine
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the wind turbine.
  - Switch on the wind turbine ON/OFF.
  - "Switch the Run/Stop selector to\_Run\_state."
  - Gradually increase the motor speed in small increments.
  - Switch to the software monitor.
  - You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
  popups:
  - afterStep: 6
    text: Always connect the battery before connecting PV panels or AC sources to
      the charge controller.
  - afterStep: 16
    text: Observe that the battery now supplies the AC load.
  - afterStep: 23
    text: You'll notice that when PV panels share the load with battery and Wind
      turbine, the battery discharge current will be reduced.
  stepItemPrefab: {fileID: 6570533322573217691, guid: cd25d304eaf4809488e7c6b299d13404, type: 3}
  contentParent: {fileID: 33731101}
